# No backwards compatibility by default

Prefect is **pre-stability / in development**. Prefer the clean shape over compatibility layers. See ADR-0018.

## Default

- Breaking renames, interface changes, Manifest/State/schema churn, and Host-side path moves are **OK** unless something is explicitly marked stable or external.
- Do **not** add dual-read, dual-write, migration shims, deprecation aliases, or "just in case" compat code.
- When changing a contract, update callers, tests, docs, and glossary in the same change. Leave no transitional half-life.

## Exceptions (rare)

Maintain compatibility only when the user says so, or when the surface is clearly external (e.g. a published operator contract already relied on outside this repo). If unsure, ask — do not invent a compatibility path.

## Examples

```text
❌ Keep old Manifest key `state` and also read `intent`
✅ Rename to `intent`; update every Manifest and reader in one change

❌ Wrapper that accepts both old and new Host Volume paths
✅ Move to the new path; update Setup and tests together
```
